      "heading": "Annex 1: Action plan addressing AI-enabled cybersecurity threats",
      "section_kind": "annex",
      "body": "The six focus areas follow Annex 1 of the ECB's letter. Areas 1 to 4 are short-term; areas 5 and 6 are structural.\n\n| Focus area | Measures | Accountable function | Due date |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1. Protecting the attack surface | 1.1 Inventory of internet-facing assets and software components\n1.2 Removal of 14 unused third-party VPN connections | Head of IT Infrastructure | 31 Dec 2026\n31 Jan 2027 |\n| 2. Vulnerability and patch management | 2.1 Daily risk-based scanning of internet-facing assets\n2.2 Emergency change procedure for critical patches | CISO | 30 Nov 2026\n31 Jan 2027 |\n| 3. Monitoring and detection | 3.1 Log coverage for all internet-facing applications in the SOC | Head of Security Operations | 31 Mar 2027 |\n| 4. Governance, funding and supply chain | 4.1 Patching terms with critical ICT service providers\n4.2 Risk appetite metric for patching latency | CRO | 31 Mar 2027\nDone, 21 Oct 2026 |\n| 5. Defence in depth and modernisation | 5.1 Replacement of the end-of-life payment gateway | CIO | 30 Sep 2027 |\n| 6. Response and recovery | 6.1 Crisis exercise on a zero-day compromise of a perimeter device | Head of Business Continuity | 30 Jun 2027 |",
